{"chapter": "sites", "node_kind": "proposition", "parent_tag": "00W1", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{F} \\to \\mathcal{F}^\\#$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{F} \\to \\mathcal{G}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{G}$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{F}^\\# \\to \\mathcal{G}$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{F} \\to \\mathcal{F}^\\#\n\\to \\mathcal{G}$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proposition}\n\\label{proposition-sheafification-adjoint}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proposition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:6c2d7377a8af2bed05424ae055021ec8fb4899835a12e442a07963cad02d3de7", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:f79f1513b3e36daceaf9b27f3096803ca94d092aff688c746c082f9df8560f3a", "source_text": "The canonical map <MATH_0001> has the\nfollowing universal property: For any map <MATH_0002>,\nwhere <MATH_0003> is a sheaf of sets, there is a unique map\n<MATH_0004> such that <MATH_0005> equals the given map.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:80e235bd9bcde2f9596ffb357e85b670bb4bcd39158a053128f1ef0f582fc322", "unit_id": "tag:00WH:statement"}
{"chapter": "sites", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "00W1", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\n\\mathcal{F} \\ar[r] \\ar[d]\n&\n\\mathcal{F}^{+} \\ar[r] \\ar[d]\n&\n\\mathcal{F}^{++} \\ar[d]\n\\\\\n\\mathcal{G} \\ar[r]\n&\n\\mathcal{G}^{+} \\ar[r]\n&\n\\mathcal{G}^{++}\n}\n$$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{F}^\\#$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-plus-functorial}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{theorem-plus}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{lemma-plus-surjective}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:d52167a3eccd45050a679c65711862d707dd1b702d37d3133569d0fdaff2fd40", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:5b632e0d725a28bb75c9ca26a17959d3431c43e954fa06e9e5a4931820e587af", "source_text": "By Lemma <REF_0001> we get a commutative diagram\n<MATH_0001>\nand by Theorem <REF_0002> the lower horizontal maps\nare isomorphisms. The uniqueness follows from Lemma\n<REF_0003> which says that every section of\n<MATH_0002> locally comes from sections of <MATH_0003>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:f704e5bc66409ccf9ff7e02395072f0333fc9ab4ea6c0eb12661b1fcd77b86da", "unit_id": "tag:00WH:proof"}
{"chapter": "sites", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "00W1", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{F}\n\\mapsto (\\mathcal{F} \\to \\mathcal{F}^\\#)$", "MATH_0002": "$i : \\Sh(\\mathcal{C}) \\to \\textit{PSh}(\\mathcal{C})$", "MATH_0003": "$$\n\\Mor_{\\textit{PSh}(\\mathcal{C})}(\\mathcal{F}, i(\\mathcal{G}))\n=\n\\Mor_{\\Sh(\\mathcal{C})}(\\mathcal{F}^\\#, \\mathcal{G}).\n$$", "MATH_0004": "$i$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:2370fafea63d7273dcd9dc32c763806ca3be4d3243f312aa63365161cd1a386a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:e4f52ac070a1fa60457fd0729525cd219f255c11ed272ed2db9ac044aeddf65c", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nIt is clear from this result that the functor <MATH_0001> is unique\nup to unique isomorphism of functors. Actually, let us temporarily\ndenote <MATH_0002>\nthe functor of inclusion. The result above actually says that\n<MATH_0003>\nIn other words, the functor of sheafification is the left adjoint\nto the inclusion functor <MATH_0004>.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:1ba1907d9fed2e68f95bd14286f462b8ae0b5777a63cb02499a75d1a7ba012e1", "unit_id": "tag:00W1:prose-0006"}
{"chapter": "sites", "node_kind": "example", "parent_tag": "00W1", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0002": "$E$", "MATH_0003": "$\\underline{E}$", "MATH_0004": "$E$", "MATH_0005": "$E$", "MATH_0006": "$\\Mor_{\\Sh(\\mathcal{C})}(\\underline{E}, \\mathcal{F}) =\n\\Mor_{\\textit{Sets}}(E, \\Gamma(\\mathcal{C}, \\mathcal{F}))$", "MATH_0007": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0008": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{definition-global-sections}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{example}\n\\label{example-constant-sheaf}\n", "suffix": "\\end{example}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:8919e7a5ce6f24c8fc82f87fe51ef7d303bc639076466a70563ea2f244e17716", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:73b8de44d2a2ebec3289a1e90e22a62ca9e87ae2b7c6b0c8af487f5e26bffd55", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a site. Let <MATH_0002> be a set.\nThe <TEXTITOPEN_0001>constant sheaf <MATH_0003> with value <MATH_0004><TEXTITCLOSE_0001>\nis the sheafification of the presheaf given by the constant\nfunctor with value <MATH_0005>. It is characterized by the rule\n<MATH_0006>\nfor every sheaf <MATH_0007> on <MATH_0008> where the\nnotation is from Definition <REF_0001>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:93d20c93da86165f4e147188e89d7c8d134fb1aafbb17b0a3be07ad1904beac0", "unit_id": "tag:0H7J:statement"}
{"chapter": "sites", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "00W1", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:7013008b7dbaa7c3ba94b406de0149cddf21bed360bbc46e62d10adffe6eac67", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nWe finish this section with a couple of lemmas.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:322493916ce2a612ce8ff0d3cb08ac2be6e74e4f0571e31d317a90f9f8bda2ff", "unit_id": "tag:00W1:prose-0007"}
{"chapter": "sites", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "00W1", "placeholders": {"LOCKED_0001": "\\begin{slogan}\nColimit in category of sheaves equals sheafification of colimit in\ncategory of presheaves.\n\\end{slogan}", "MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{F} : \\mathcal{I} \\to \\Sh(\\mathcal{C})$", "MATH_0002": "$\\colim_\\mathcal{I} \\mathcal{F}$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-colimit-sheaves}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:8a1b0c48158f3b7fa8d5a5b027c66b4076b9524c155bc372300f656cdb0d15b2", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:3baae08fe786b231a4e0f59a3379faabca0f58f0c867d9fd7a880d255c44eee8", "source_text": "<LOCKED_0001>\nLet <MATH_0001>\nbe a diagram. Then <MATH_0002> exists\nand is the sheafification of the colimit in the category of presheaves.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:891edc732c21c1a8e94b8f95ccbd9076675bef5cf8f980595bca910ca7d1a7ae", "unit_id": "tag:00WI:statement"}
{"chapter": "sites", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "00W1", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\textit{PSh}(\\mathcal{C})$", "MATH_0002": "$\\Sh(\\mathcal{C})$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{categories-lemma-adjoint-exact}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:eacbcb9e66a080aa208738b0d8668ea2c2ac6f9b2510f9c2ad8832188bceb5b9", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:b12dc3381e3060be72c41a1c9ba169ad25530000cf00a2a45c2bad3195f572b8", "source_text": "Since the sheafification functor is a left adjoint it commutes\nwith all colimits, see Categories,\nLemma <REF_0001>.\nHence, since <MATH_0001> has colimits, we deduce\nthat <MATH_0002> has colimits (which are the\nsheafifications of the colimits in presheaves).\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:921885f1b5d6c8df9c199549eea413ebe1723cac02bc31d60061935ab56089a7", "unit_id": "tag:00WI:proof"}
{"chapter": "sites", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "00W1", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\textit{PSh}(\\mathcal{C}) \\to \\Sh(\\mathcal{C})$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{F} \\mapsto \\mathcal{F}^\\#$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-sheafification-exact}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:f3db79a09fd4101c48ed5b182eeb40e3f210909a131de67f6150d48f297ae80d", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:127fedceb4c8b574fb998bdfab37d55fd903195af625758e56702dc073cb698b", "source_text": "The functor <MATH_0001>,\n<MATH_0002> is exact.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:43ac1621e81969b41de99737a89e4e2077f572ed190c7c6d461466ae8d617d28", "unit_id": "tag:00WJ:statement"}
{"chapter": "sites", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "00W1", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{F}^+$", "MATH_0002": "$\\Ob(\\mathcal{J}_U)$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{U} \\geq \\mathcal{U}'$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{U}$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{U}'$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{F} \\to \\mathcal{F}^+$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{categories-lemma-exact-adjoint}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-common-refinement}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{lemma-independent-refinement}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{categories-lemma-directed-commutes}", "REF_0005": "\\ref{lemma-limit-sheaf}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:b0cb2eda816c837e9005367ad90a8035d21fa6134a718d3fe9a15e06edcf8efa", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:2cb76d0eb65339caa52c58ca8ce98c94de302a4b2019cabb5fac43421e127bac", "source_text": "Since it is a left adjoint it is right exact, see\nCategories, Lemma <REF_0001>.\nOn the other hand, by Lemmas <REF_0002>\nand Lemma <REF_0003> the colimits\nin the construction of <MATH_0001> are really over the\ndirected set <MATH_0002> where\n<MATH_0003> if and only if\n<MATH_0004> is a refinement of <MATH_0005>. Hence by\nCategories, Lemma <REF_0004>\nwe see that <MATH_0006> commutes\nwith finite limits (as a functor from presheaves to\npresheaves). Then we conclude using\nLemma <REF_0005>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:e90e8a102374b081e692f201b3c55d727d52bf5391a73344d3056705bb3be7ca", "unit_id": "tag:00WJ:proof"}
